From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:07:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 169/342] Remote Control preferences: an icon; modifiers and
 every key by mouse

- An icon: Haiku's icon set has no remote control; this one is drawn by
  the project's tools/icons/remote-control-icon.py in Haiku's style.
- Alt, Ctrl, Shift and Win checkboxes (Command, Control, Shift and
  Option) next to the keystroke, and the keys the keymap types (letters,
  digits, punctuation) in the key menu: a keystroke like a music player's Alt+M
  can be made without a keyboard at the board. Picking a key keeps the
  ticked modifiers. Keystrokes are named the PC keyboard's way ("Alt+",
  "Ctrl+", "Win+").

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
